  <data key="d5">["ACQUIRED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The United States acquired control of the Panama Canal Authority.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "For most of the twentieth century the United States controlled the canal and the surrounding Canal Zone.", "chunk_id": "7bf1e0d9c075ffa9", "doc_id": "hp_ce5cb4168a3ba0d5", "type": "ACQUIRED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ce5cb4168a3ba0d5</data>
</edge>
<edge source="United States" target="Panama">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The United States controlled the canal and its surrounding area.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "For most of the twentieth century the United States controlled the canal and the surrounding Canal Zone.", "chunk_id": "7bf1e0d9c075ffa9", "doc_id": "hp_ce5cb4168a3ba0d5", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ce5cb4168a3ba0d5</data>
</edge>
<edge source="John Frank Stevens" target="Panama Canal">
  <data key="d5">["USED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">John Frank Stevens supported building a canal with locks instead of a sea-level design</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "John Frank Stevens reorganised the work and supported building a canal with locks instead of a sea-level design.", "chunk_id": "f4303e0167d12798", "doc_id": "hp_c69cf471cb591ee9", "type": "USED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_c69cf471cb591ee9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="George Washington Goethals" target="Panama Canal">
  <data key="d5">["SUCCESSOR_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">George Washington Goethals succeeded John Frank Stevens as the leader of the project to completion</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In 1907 he was succeeded by George Washington Goethals, an officer of the United States Army Corps of Engineers, who led the project to completion.", "chunk_id": "f4303e0167d12798", "doc_id": "hp_c69cf471cb591ee9", "type": "SUCCESSOR_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_c69cf471cb591ee9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="William C. Gorgas" target="Panama Canal">
  <data key="d5">["USED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">William C. Gorgas directed a sanitation campaign to control disease among the workforce</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "William C. Gorgas, a United States Army physician, directed a sanitation campaign that drained standing water, controlled mosquitoes and greatly reduced yellow fever and malaria among the workforce.", "chunk_id": "f4303e0167d12798", "doc_id": "hp_c69cf471cb591ee9", "type": "USED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_c69cf471cb591ee9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="David du Bose Gaillard" target="Panama Canal">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">David du Bose Gaillard was the engineer in charge of the Culebra Cut section of the canal and died before it opened</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The most difficult section was the Culebra Cut, a deep excavation through the continental divide. It was later renamed the Gaillard Cut after David du Bose Gaillard, the engineer in charge of that section, who died before the canal opened.", "chunk_id": "f4303e0167d12798", "doc_id": "hp_c69cf471cb591ee9", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_c69cf471cb591ee9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gatun Dam" target="Gatun Lake">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Gatun Dam created Gatun Lake</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Engineers built the Gatun Dam on the Chagres River, which created Gatun Lake.", "chunk_id": "cac1b610d8cdbd6b", "doc_id": "hp_6aa8afe67f89e68e", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6aa8afe67f89e68e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Panama" target="United States">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Panama was the recipient of control over the canal.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In 1977 United States President Jimmy Carter and Panamanian leader Omar Torrijos signed the Torrijos-Carter Treaties, which arranged for control of the canal to pass to Panama.", "chunk_id": "7bf1e0d9c075ffa9", "doc_id": "hp_ce5cb4168a3ba0d5", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ce5cb4168a3ba0d5</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Jimmy Carter" target="Panama">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Jimmy Carter was a leader of the United States.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In 1977 United States President Jimmy Carter and Panamanian leader Omar Torrijos signed the Torrijos-Carter Treaties, which arranged for control of the canal to pass to Panama.", "chunk_id": "7bf1e0d9c075ffa9", "doc_id": "hp_ce5cb4168a3ba0d5", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ce5cb4168a3ba0d5</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Omar Torrijos" target="Panama">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Omar Torrijos was a leader of Panama.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In 1977 United States President Jimmy Carter and Panamanian leader Omar Torrijos signed the Torrijos-Carter Treaties, which arranged for control of the canal to pass to Panama.", "chunk_id": "7bf1e0d9c075ffa9", "doc_id": "hp_ce5cb4168a3ba0d5", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ce5cb4168a3ba0d5</data>
</edge>
</graph></graphml>